    "this is a function call, let me explain every part of the function call, the gift “float” is the “return type” or what kind of information the function will return, the reason why I used float instead of int (integer), is because floating point variables will allow me to represent the result of such an operation, the tax value of some money will usually have a decimal part and the fractional part of a number, in other words, a number like 3.99 , needs to be a float because of the .99 part of the number… and altho the tax rate here in Japan in currently 0.8% finally amount, again, since amount can be 3.99 it again needs to be a float number. by the way tax_rare and amount are what we call “parameters to the function” they are the information the function takes in. then we see a code block. and the first instruction in the code block is the return statement… return takes the following value, evals is (calculates it) and finally gives that back to the function call. now lets take a look at some sample function calls: float candy_value=2.00; float candy_value_plus_tax; candy_value_plus_tax = calculate_tax(0.8, candy_value);//this is a function call The first line in C will setup the value of the candy, in this case 2.00 in a float variable. The second line sets up the variable which will eventually hold the value of the candy after tax. then comes the function call, first the parameters are sent tot he function so 8.0 and 2.00 are sent to the previously defined function... taking their place as tax_rate now being equal to 8.0 and amount now being equal to 2.00. then we get return amount * tax_rate. so int this specific function call, it will be like this: return 2.00*0.8; first we solve the vale of 2.00*0.8 which is 1.6 then the return statement hands that back to the function call, and sets candy_value_plus_tax to 1.6": [
      "this is a function call, let me explain every part of the function call, the gift “float” is the “return type” or what kind of information the function will return, the reason why I used float instead of int (integer), is because floating point variables will allow me to represent the result of such an operation, the tax value of some money will usually have a decimal part and the fractional part of a number, in other words, a number like 3.99 , needs to be a float because of the .99 part of the number… and altho the tax rate here in Japan in currently 0.8% finally amount, again, since amount can be 3.99 it again needs to be a float number. by the way tax_rare and amount are what we call “parameters to the function” they are the information the function takes in. then we see a code block. and the first instruction in the code block is the return statement… return takes the following value, evals is (calculates it) and finally gives that back to the function call. now lets take a look at some sample function calls: float candy_value=2.00; float candy_value_plus_tax; candy_value_plus_tax = calculate_tax(0.8, candy_value);//this is a function call The first line in C will setup the value of the candy, in this case 2.00 in a float variable. The second line sets up the variable which will eventually hold the value of the candy after tax. then comes the function call, first the parameters are sent tot he function so 8.0 and 2.00 are sent to the previously defined function... taking their place as tax_rate now being equal to 8.0 and amount now being equal to 2.00. then we get return amount * tax_rate. so int this specific function call, it will be like this: return 2.00*0.8; first we solve the vale of 2.00*0.8 which is 1.6 then the return statement hands that back to the function call, and sets candy_value_plus_tax to 1.6",
      "これは関数呼び出しです,関数の呼び出しのすべての部分を説明しましょう,ギフト  ⁇ float ⁇ は  ⁇  return type ⁇  または関数が返される情報の種類です. int (整数) の代わりに float を使った理由は,浮点変数はそのような操作の結果を表示できるようにするためです.ある貨幣の税値には通常,10分の部分があり,数字の割引部分があります. コードブロックは返済式です...返却式は次の値を取ります, evals は (それを計算します) そして最後に関数呼び出しに返します. さて,いくつかのサンプル関数呼び出しを見てみましょう: float candy_value=2.00; float candy_value_plus_tax; candy_value_plus_tax = calculate_tax(0.8, candy_value);//これは関数呼び出しです C の最初の行は,浮動変数で candy の値を設定します. 次に関数呼び出しがやってきます. まずパラメータは函数に送信されるので,8.0と2.00は以前に定義された関数に送信されます. その代わり,税率が8.0に等しくなり,金額が2.00に等しくなります.",
      "esto es una llamada de la función, permítanme explicar cada parte de la llamada de la función, el regalo “float” es el “tipo de retorno” o qué tipo de información la función va a devolver, la razón por la que usé flotador en lugar de int (integer), es porque las variables de punto flotante me permitirán representar el resultado de tal operación, el valor tributario de algún dinero generalmente tendrá una parte decimal y la parte fraccional de un número actual, como . por la forma tax_rare y la cantidad son lo que llamamos “parameters a la función” son la información que toma la función. entonces vemos un bloque de código. y la primera instrucción en el bloque de código es la declaración de retorno... devolver toma el siguiente valor, evals es (la calcula) y finalmente da eso de vuelta a la llamada de función. ahora vamos a echar un vistazo a algunas llamadas de la función de muestra: flotador candy_value=2.00; flotador candy_value_plus_tax; candy_value_plus_tax = calculate_tax(0.8, candy_value);/ / esta es una llamada de la función La primera línea en C establecerá el valor del caramelo, en este caso 2.00 en una variable flotante. La segunda línea establece la variable que eventualmente mantendrá el valor de los caramelos después del impuesto. entonces viene la llamada de función, primero los parámetros se envían tot que funciona para que 8.0 y 2.00 sean enviados a la función previamente definida... tomar su lugar como tax_rate ahora siendo igual a 8.0 y la cantidad ahora es igual a 2.00. entonces obtenemos la cantidad de devolución * tax_rate. así que int esta llamada de función específica, será como esto: devolver 2.00*0.8; primero resolvemos el vale de 2.00*0.8 que es 1.6 luego las manos de declaración de retorno que de vuelta a la llamada de la función, y establece candy_value_plus_tax a 1.6"
    ],
